      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T16:30:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would call this simply `advance`. All the call sites look the same:\n```\n    auto range \u003d getNextRange();\n    mOffset \u003d range.first;\n    mSize \u003d range.second;\n```\nso you can also move the mOffset and mSize setting into this function. I would also shift mBits so that the 0th bit is at offset+size. We would store:\n\n * current offset\n * current size\n * bits that have been shifted to offset + size and are ready to have `advance` called again.\n \nWe could probably avoid needing `mWordOffset` because the bits we want to look at always start at the first bit.\n \nThis means that the iterator will be comparable to the `end` iterator without any processing once there are no ranges left.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 131,
        "startChar": 67,
        "endLine": 131,
        "endChar": 79
      },
      "revId": "fe2d8b910f2edee414bfffbffa6d4a10120df254",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
