      "side": 1,
      "message": "ANGLE has overloads for ScanForward [0] which work on 64 bits with fallbacks for 32-bit systems. Using those would likely be much faster since we do have a bunch of bitsets in the 32-64 bit size. You would use `to_ullong` instead to get the values out of the std::bitset.\n\n[0] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/third_party/angle/src/common/mathutil.h;l\u003d1220-1240;drc\u003df5196a27b9b6bdc358191717f2b5a3ba824d1e82 and https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/third_party/angle/src/common/mathutil.h;l\u003d1283-1293;drc\u003df5196a27b9b6bdc358191717f2b5a3ba824d1e82",
