      "writtenOn": "2025-03-21T16:30:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we can avoid the loop here. If we invert `remainingBits` then we can use ScanForward on it again to find the next `0` bit.\n\nThe algorithm then becomes roughly:\n```\noffset \u003d ScanForward(bits)\nbits \u003d bits \u003e\u003e offset\nbits \u003d ~bits\nsize \u003d ScanForward(bits) // Here we need to handle wrapping to the next word, we will know because there will be a 1 bit at the end of our data due to the ~\nbits \u003d bits \u003e\u003e size\nbits \u003d ~bits\n```\n\nI would refactor some of these into helper functions that are marked inline. Something like `uint32_t findNext1Bit()` which handles the word wrapping would help a lot here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 142,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 147,
        "endChar": 13
      },
      "revId": "fe2d8b910f2edee414bfffbffa6d4a10120df254",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
